   "source": [
    "# Retail Outlet Data Visualisation\n",
    "\n",
    "Exploratory and interactive analysis of daily customer visits across 45 retail outlets, supported by outlet-level business characteristics including marketing spend, overheads, floor space and staffing.\n",
    "\n",
    "This portfolio version focuses on reproducible analysis, clear visual communication and business interpretation. The original coursework identifiers and university submission material have been removed.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Project goals\n",
    "\n",
    "- Compare annual customer traffic across outlets.\n",
    "- Identify potential outlet openings and closures from time-series behaviour.\n",
    "- Examine visit distributions and correlations between higher-volume outlets.\n",
    "- Explore relationships between customer visits and commercial drivers such as marketing, overheads, floor space and staffing.\n",
    "- Demonstrate both static and interactive visualisation techniques.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data\n",
    "\n",
    "The original dataset was supplied for academic coursework and is **not redistributed in this public portfolio repository**. To run the notebook locally, place the five source CSV files in `../data/` using the filenames shown in the loading cell below.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import hvplot.pandas\n",
    "import holoviews as hv\n",
    "\n",
    "hv.extension(\"bokeh\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DATA_DIR = \"../data\"\n",
    "\n",
    "data = pd.read_csv(f\"{DATA_DIR}/OutletDailyCustomers.csv\", index_col=0)\n",
    "data.index = pd.to_datetime(data.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "outlet_marketing = pd.read_csv(f\"{DATA_DIR}/OutletMarketing.csv\", index_col=0)\n",
    "outlet_overhead = pd.read_csv(f\"{DATA_DIR}/OutletOverheads.csv\", index_col=0)\n",
    "outlet_size = pd.read_csv(f\"{DATA_DIR}/OutletSize.csv\", index_col=0)\n",
    "outlet_staff = pd.read_csv(f\"{DATA_DIR}/OutletStaff.csv\", index_col=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(data.shape)\n",
    "display(data.head())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "summary_data = pd.DataFrame(index=data.columns)\n",
    "summary_data[\"Marketing\"] = outlet_marketing.loc[data.columns].values\n",
    "summary_data[\"Overhead\"] = outlet_overhead.loc[data.columns].values\n",
    "summary_data[\"Size Outlet\"] = outlet_size.loc[data.columns].values\n",
    "summary_data[\"Amount Staff\"] = outlet_staff.loc[data.columns].values\n",
    "summary_data[\"Annual Visits\"] = data.sum().values\n",
    "\n",
    "display(summary_data.head())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Annual customer visits by outlet\n",
    "\n",
    "Outlets are segmented by annual visit volume to make the distribution easier to interpret.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "display_data",
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x700 with 1 Axes>"
      ],
      "image/png": "\n"
     },
     "metadata": {}
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "total_visits = data.sum()\n",
    "segment_limits = {\n",
    "    0: 'Very Low',\n",
    "    10_000: 'Low',\n",
    "    200_000: 'Medium',\n",
    "    500_000: 'High',\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "segment_colours = {\n",
    "    'Very Low': 'purple',\n",
    "    'Low': 'hotpink',\n",
    "    'Medium': 'pink',\n",
    "    'High': 'plum',\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def get_segment(value):\n",
    "    if value >= 500_000:\n",
    "        return 'High'\n",
    "    elif value >= 200_000:\n",
    "        return 'Medium'\n",
    "    elif value >= 10_000:\n",
    "        return 'Low'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'Very Low'\n",
    "\n",
    "total_visits_sorted = total_visits.sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "colours = [segment_colours[get_segment(value)] for value in total_visits_sorted]\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 7))\n",
    "x_pos = np.arange(len(total_visits_sorted))\n",
    "plt.bar(x_pos, total_visits_sorted.values, align='center', color=colours)\n",
    "plt.xticks(x_pos, total_visits_sorted.index, rotation=90)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Outlets', fontsize=18)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Annual Visits', fontsize=18)\n",
    "plt.title('Annual Customer Visits per Outlet (High to Low)', fontsize=20)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
